# Issue #2198: secretlint has been a devDependency since the log-sanitizer
# landed, but nothing ever ran it, so CI could not catch a committed secret.
# The scan is fail-closed now; these are the only paths exempted, and each is
# exempt because holding a *fake* secret is the file's entire purpose.
#
# Keep this list minimal. Never add a path just to make the scan pass -- if a
# real credential lands anywhere else, the lint job must fail.

# Fixtures for the log sanitizer. src/*.lib.mjs runs secretlint's own API over
# solve/hive logs before they are attached to a pull request; these tests feed
# it synthetic tokens and assert the output no longer contains them. Removing
# the tokens would delete the thing under test.
tests/test-token-sanitization.mjs
tests/test-credential-sanitization-2111.mjs
tests/test-telegram-auth-command.mjs
tests/test-issue-2189-sentry-log-sanitization.mjs

# Same, for the throwaway scripts that reproduced the sanitizer bugs.
experiments/test-secretlint-api.mjs
experiments/issue-2156-*.mjs

# Archived evidence. Case-study logs are verbatim captures of real runs kept
# for post-mortems; their credentials were already redacted at capture time
# (`gho_REDACTED_TOKEN`) or are prose describing a URL shape we rejected.
docs/case-studies/**
